questions.q:
The locus of the point $P(x, y)$ satisfying the relation
$\begin{aligned}
& \sqrt{(x-3)^2+(y-1)^2} \\
& \quad+\sqrt{(x+3)^2+(y-1)^2}=6 \text{ is }
\end{aligned}$

questions.solution:
Obtain the foot of the perpendicular $N(-4,1,-3)$.
Find the equations of the line passing through
$\begin{aligned}
& P(2,4,-1) \text{ and } N(-4,1,-3) \\
& \qquad \frac{x-2}{6}=\frac{y-4}{3}=\frac{z+1}{2}
\end{aligned}$
